From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:11:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: click a reaction to join it, reactions list moves
 into message info

Clicking a reaction pill under a message now sends that emoji as your own
reaction, or takes it back when it is already yours (one reaction per
contact, as everywhere else in the UI). The "+N" overflow pill and the
keyboard-reachable button behind the pills open the message info dialog
instead of the separate Reactions dialog.

The Reactions dialog is gone: its contact list (avatar, name, emoji,
click-through to the profile) now renders as a "Reactions" section at the
end of the message info dialog, after read receipts and attachment details,
so who-reacted and who-read live in one place.

Rebased onto v2.62.0: upstream rewrote the Reactions dialog meanwhile
(49a33099d, aaf99cad2, ee7433f49, 0a31d3a6a: emoji pills that toggle
your reaction, a total count, live updates). This patch still removes
it, since the pills under the message toggle directly and the
who-reacted list lives in Message Info, so upstream's dialog code
(pills, live refresh) is deleted with it and its stylesheet loses the
pill classes. Reactions keeps upstream's render-all and visually-hidden
overflow (781bedd9f). ReactionsBar's doc-link import of the deleted
dialog is dropped too.
